mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Koperasi Backend API\n\nBackend canister for a cooperative (koperasi) management application. It stores\nmembers, chart of accounts (COA), savings, loans, installments, journals, user\naccounts, and dashboard state, and exposes the public methods documented below.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\nThe canister does **not** use Internet Identity for its own login. Instead it\nmaintains an application-level session:\n\n- `login(username, password)` verifies the credentials and stores the matching\n  user id in the canister's single `currentSession` slot.\n- `logout()` clears that slot.\n- Every other method reads the session to decide the caller's cooperative role\n  (`#admin`, `#kasir`, `#supervisor`).\n\nBecause the session is a single canister-wide slot, it is **not** per-principal:\nthe `caller` principal is ignored by `login`, and the last successful login\ndetermines the session for all subsequent calls until `logout()` or another\n`login`. Do not treat the caller principal as an identity boundary here.\n\nThe frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at\n`/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the\nuser's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal\nagainst that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`).\nSuch a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it\nexpires.\n\n### Roles and authorization\n\nRoles are `#admin`, `#kasir`, `#supervisor`. The seeded account is\n`admin` / `admin123` with role `#admin`.\n\nOnly these methods enforce a role, and they enforce it from the session:\n\n- `createUserAccount` — admin session only; otherwise `#err(\"Hanya admin yang dapat membuat akun\")`.\n- `assignUserRole` — admin session only; otherwise `#err(\"Hanya admin yang dapat mengubah hak akses\")`.\n- `closeMonth` / `closeYear` — admin session only; otherwise `#err(\"Hanya admin yang dapat menutup bulan\")` / `#err(\"Hanya admin yang dapat menutup tahun\")`.\n- `clearTransactionData` — admin session only, plus the exact confirmation text `HAPUS`; otherwise `#err(\"Hanya admin yang dapat membersihkan data\")` or `#err(\"Konfirmasi salah. Ketik HAPUS untuk melanjutkan.\")`.\n\nAll other methods (`createMember`, `createAccount`, `recordSavingsTransaction`,\n`createLoan`, `postManualJournal`, `uploadLogo`, …) do **not** check a role and\nare callable by any caller, including anonymous. They are not access-controlled.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- All monetary amounts (`principal`, `amount`, `balance`, `debit`, `credit`,\n  `remainingPrincipal`, `interestRate`, `penaltyRate`) are `Float`. Interest and\n  penalty rates are expressed as percentages (for example `5.0` = 5%).\n- Timestamps (`joinedAt`, `createdAt`, `disbursedAt`, `paidAt`) are `Nat`\n  nanoseconds since the Unix epoch, as returned by `Time.now()`.\n- Ids (`MemberId`, `LoanId`, `SavingsId`, `JournalId`, `UserId`) are `Nat`.\n  `AccountCode` and `TransactionNumber` are `Text`.\n- `Result<T>` is `{ #ok : T; #err : Text }`. Errors are plain Indonesian text,\n  not a structured variant — a caller must string-match to distinguish them.\n- The seeded Kas account code is `\"100\"`. `getCashFlow` and `getCashFlow30Days`\n  read account `\"100\"` specifically.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- `postMonthlySavingsInterest()` and `postMonthlyLoanInterest()` are **manual**\n  update calls. There is no time-based trigger in the canister; a scheduler or\n  operator must invoke them. Each returns `#ok(count)` of the entries posted.\n- `sendDueReminders()` is a manual update call that sends H-3 due reminders by\n  email; it returns `#ok(count)`.\n- `closeMonth(period)` / `closeYear(period)` record a period close in dashboard\n  state. They are idempotent in effect only in that they overwrite the stored\n  close record; they do not lock or freeze any data.\n- Reports (`getTrialBalance`, `getIncomeStatement`, `getBalanceSheet`, `getShu`,\n  `getCashFlow`, `getLedger`) are computed on read from the current journals and\n  accounts, so they are always up to date.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- Most create methods allocate a new id from a counter and are **not**\n  idempotent: retrying `createMember`, `createLoan`, `createSavingsType`,\n  `createAccount`, `postManualJournal`, or `postCashEntry` creates a duplicate.\n- `recordSavingsTransaction` and `recordInstallment` append a new transaction\n  each call; retrying duplicates the transaction.\n- `clearTransactionData` is destructive: it clears all journals, savings\n  transactions, and installments. It requires the exact confirmation `HAPUS`.\n- `importInitialSavingsBalances` overwrites the balance for each supplied\n  `(memberId, savingsTypeId)` pair, so re-running it is safe for the same rows.\n- `uploadLogo` overwrites the stored logo URL.\n\n## Errors, traps, and gotchas\n\n- `postCashEntry` rejects unbalanced lines with\n  `#err(\"Total debit dan kredit harus seimbang\")` and empty lines with\n  `#err(\"Kas harus memiliki minimal satu baris\")`.\n- `changeOwnPassword` returns `#err(\"Belum login\")` when there is no session.\n- `createUserAccount` returns `#err(\"Username sudah digunakan\")` on a duplicate\n  username.\n- `calculatePenalty` returns `#err(\"Pinjaman tidak ditemukan\")` for an unknown\n  loan.\n- `getCallerRole` returns `null` when there is no session.\n- `getLogo` returns the empty string when no logo was uploaded.\n- `backupDatabase` returns a JSON text snapshot of members, accounts, and\n  journals; it is a read, not a file.\n- The session is global, not per-caller: concurrent users of the same canister\n  share one session. This is a single-operator design.\n\n## OQL data access\n\nThe canister exposes its persisted collections through the Caffeine OQL\n`schema()` and `execute()` methods. Registered entities: `member`, `account`,\n`savingsType`, `savingsTransaction`, `loan`, `installment`, and `journal`. All\nare `controllerOnly` — readable by the platform controller, not by end users.\n"
  };
};
